(5.4-6.2% vs 3.1-4.7%) and the effect is not monotonic - 640 beats 960 on scale, twice. Low-resolution
arms repeat to within 0.03 cm / 0.03 points; the 1920 arm's own scale spread is 1.6 points, so its "3.07%"
is not a reliable floor. Under the stated gate (scale must stay inside the full-resolution spread) neither
downscaled arm passes. CPU seconds fall only 38% for 9x fewer pixels, so the front end is not the whole
replay cost.
